Now the claude adapter's discover: an over-cap file on a NON-ranged backend currently vanishes (`_firstCwd` → '' → cwd-match fails). On ranged backends it's discovered (uncapped 4096 prefix) and refuses at read time.

The omp adapter: same — ranged discovers, non-ranged vanishes (`_readHeader` → null → continue).

The parity fix (thread 26, mirrored per "check same pattern across codebase"):

**claude_adapter.dart discover:**
```dart
for (final (path, size, mtimeMs) in await listSessionFiles(fs, bucketPath)) {
  final headerCwd = await _firstCwd(fs, path, maxFileBytes: limits.maxFileBytes);
  // An over-cap file cannot be probed within the cap on backends without
  // partial reads (headerCwd comes back ''); it still becomes a summary
  // — unverified cwd — so scanForeignLines' read-time refusal produces
  // the counted `file too large` warning, the same flow the ranged
  // prefix read already gives (GOAL E11 reporting parity).
  final overCap = headerCwd.isEmpty && size > limits.maxFileBytes;
  if (headerCwd.isNotEmpty && !headerCwdMatches(headerCwd, cwd)) continue;
  if (headerCwd.isEmpty && !overCap) continue;
