```

Hmm wait, careful. Current logic: `if (!headerCwdMatches(headerCwd, cwd)) continue;` — and headerCwdMatches returns false for empty headerCwd. So current: headerCwd '' → skip. New logic needs: 
- headerCwd non-empty: match → include; no-match → skip.
- headerCwd empty: include ONLY if overCap.

So:
```dart
if (headerCwd.isEmpty) {
  // Over the cap there is no safe probe on non-ranged backends — keep
  // the summary so the read-time refusal warns with the size reason.
  if (size <= limits.maxFileBytes) continue;
} else if (!headerCwdMatches(headerCwd, cwd)) {
  continue;
}
```

That's clean and preserves every existing behavior except the non-ranged over-cap vanish.

Also note: ranged over-cap files — _firstCwd reads prefix fine → real cwd → matched → included. Unchanged. ✓

**omp_adapter.dart discover** (mirror):
Current:
```dart
