Now I have the full picture. The runner catches `ForeignFileError` per summary and emits `warning: skipped <sourceId>: file too large: ...` — the counted warning. So if discovery includes the over-cap summary, the flow produces exactly what the reviewer asked for: `warning: skipped <id>: file too large (limit ...)`.

