```

And an end-to-end flavor through runImport asserting the warning line — that pins the "counted warning" story the thread asks for. Where do runner IT tests live? import_runner_test.dart. I could add the runImport-level test there with the non-ranged env... but runImport also needs the repo (JsonlSessionRepo with a ranged or non-ranged fs? JsonlSessionRepo needs to WRITE; a non-ranged wrapper still supports writes since FileSystem has write methods — fine).

Hmm, keep it focused: UT-tier tests in the adapter tier (discover refuses at read). Plus one runner-level test asserting the emitted warning line — that's the exact user-visible behavior from the thread ("`fa import --all` reports ... instead of omp's `warning: skipped <id>: file too large`"). Let me check how import_runner_test.dart drives runImport to reuse its helpers.

